\newlabel{fig:gradient_cosine_across_envs}{{5}{10}{\textbf {Gradient Accuracy}: We compare the ground truth gradient of $E$ with three sampled variants: October 8, which uses raw returns and suffers from double sampling; Forward Only which drops the backward term, incurring bias; and V Aux, which uses an auxiliary network in the backward term. The cosine similarity varies between $1$ (directional alignment), to $-1$, full misalignment, and is $0$ when the gradients are orthogonal}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:gradient_cosine_across_envs@cref}{{[figure][5][]5}{[1][7][]10}}
